From 55175b1a7694aedf8754eb15ef54190e895a0343 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dwong <dowling.wong@kit.edu>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 18:37:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] T22: correct a mislabelled point summary and add a
 zero-fit recombine stage

hierarchical_file_bootstrap reported the equal-file mean of each file's
BOOTSTRAP mean under the field name equal_file_mean_of_point_estimates.  The
label was wrong, not the inference: intervals, p-values, Holm adjustment and all
three verdicts are unchanged, and the two summaries differ only by the
bootstrap's small bias (+0.39202 vs +0.392717 on Delta(zero, band-EMPCA)).

The function now takes the observed per-file estimates explicitly and reports
both quantities under their own names; without them the estimand field is NaN
rather than a silently substituted bootstrap quantity, and a regression test
asserts both.

A 'recombine' stage reads an archived hold-out stage output and its draw arrays
and recomputes the combined block.  It opens no data file and fits nothing
(fits_performed: 0), so it is post-processing and not a second evaluation of the
frozen hold-out.  Run once per stage into T22_validation_v2 and
T22_final_test_v2; the v1 outputs are left untouched.

32 tests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
